cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "BdG eigensolver, self-consistency solvers, validation scripts, and data for self-consistent EM feedback in Majorana nanowires"
authors:
  - family-names: Rohilla
    given-names: Arnav
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5513-479X"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Colorado, USA"
abstract: >-
  Source code, validation scripts, raw numerical results and methods notes accompanying the paper "Self-consistent
  electromagnetic feedback in Majorana nanowires: a validated single-channel null result, and its breakdown beyond one
  subband". The repository contains a particle-hole-symmetric Bogoliubov-de Gennes (BdG) eigensolver, a real-space
  Pfaffian Z2 topological detector, a Biot-Savart ring self-field, the self-consistent feedback solvers and their
  extensions (wire length and inductance, reactive impedance, finite temperature, disorder and multiple transverse
  subbands), the validation scripts for each of these, the raw numerical results and figures, and methods notes that
  record each calculation, its validation gates and its corrections, including superseded results, which are kept and
  marked as such. Developed with the assistance of AI coding tools; all results were verified by the author using the
  validation gates described in the paper.
keywords:
  - Majorana
  - topological superconductivity
  - Bogoliubov-de Gennes
  - self-consistent feedback
  - Pfaffian invariant
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MidnightNotHere/majorana-nanowire-em-feedback"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
